 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with pauses of 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds before
+successive retries. If all attempts time out, the final `GatewayTimeout` is raised. The pauses can add up to
+20 seconds to the member's wait on the confirmation page, in addition to the time spent calling the gateway.
+
+The previous 3 attempts ran back to back within a second, so all could fall in the same slow minute during the
+gateway's Friday peak, 17:00 to 19:00. One Friday, 58 confirmed pantry orders went uncharged and a volunteer captured
+them by hand the next morning. Replaying those timeouts against the sandbox with the new schedule would have
+recovered 57 of the 58. The maintainer accepted the longer confirmation-page wait to reduce manual captures;
+switching gateways was deferred because the contract runs to December 2026. These findings and the accepted
+tradeoff are recorded in [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md).
 
